ole file's own `next` review requests (added in `buildWorker`) always bypass `when:`. Test both.\n6. **Changed-path range (bug).** `localRef(jb.branch)` (`refs/ard/<branch>`) exists only for a branch that was fetched at the start of the job. On a new branch it does not exist, and after this job's push it is stale.\n   - Record the pushed head in `push()` (`jb.head = res.SHA`). Use `s.h.BaseSHA` for the no-code path in `round`.\n   - Compute changed paths as `ChangedPaths(RepoDir, MergeBase(RepoDir, jb.cfg.SHA, head), head)`. `MergeBase` is already on the worker `Git` interface.\n   - `finishWithPR` reaches `openPR` too, so use `jb.head` there as well.\n   - If `head` is empty or all zeros (a dry-run `CommitCode` returns a synthetic zero SHA), skip git and fail open without a warning.\n7. **Renames and deletions.** `git diff --name-only` uses rename detection by default (`diff.renames`), so a rename lists only the new path. A move out of `web/` would then miss a `web/` rule. Add `--no-renames` to `gitx.ChangedPaths`, so a rename lists both old and new paths. This only makes the committer's declared-path check stricter. Add a gitx test (rename lists both paths, a deletion is listed), and run the committer tests. Deleted paths count as changed.\n8. **Exclude all of `.ard/`, not just `excluded()`.** The reviewer's `diff.patch` excludes `:(top,exclude).ard/`, and the diff guard bars any other `.ard/` path on a worker branch. Drop every path under `.ard/` (and `.ard-input/`) before matching, so a reviewer is never selected by a close-out file. Note in the docs that `when.paths` cannot select on `.ard/`.\n9. **\"A triage role ran.\"** A role counts as having run when either source shows it:\n   - a closed, done triage close-out in state (the plan's `closeout.TriageRoles`), or\n   - the issue carries `ard:triage:<role>:done`, read from `jb.is.Labels` through `labels.Done`.\n\n   The union keeps the rule working after `ard rebuild-state` and matches the #45 test plan, which uses the label. A needs-human or failed triage does not count (Q2). If the store read errors, fall back to the labels alone and log `worker.reviewers_failed`.\n10. **Selection is monotonic across pushes.** Every worker run (a re-claim, or a #41 fix round) recomputes the set from the whole PR diff (merge base to head). Close-out only adds request labels and never removes one, so a reviewer requested earlier stays requested even when later commits no longer match. A reviewer that starts to match on a later push is added. Put this sentence in the proposal and the `reviewers` doc comment. Add a worker test: run 1 does not touch `go.mod`, so license-review is not requested; run 2 on the same branch adds `go.mod`, so it is requested; eng-review is not duplicated.\n11. **Empty selection.** If reviewer roles exist but none is selected, log `worker.no_reviewers` at Warn with the issue and PR. Do not change gates. `prgate.Labels` returns `ReasonNoReviews` and `maybeReady` leaves the PR a draft for a human. Say so in the proposal.\n12. **Fail open, precisely.** When git fails, every role whose `Paths` is non-empty is treated as matched; triage still uses whatever it could read. Log one `worker.reviewers_failed` with a `step` attribute (`merge_base`, `changed_paths` or `triage`). Add tests for a git error and a store error.\n13. **Docs.**\n    - `docs/proposal.md` step 8 (line ~305): drop \"`when:` rules are ignored until #42\" and state the rules from 3, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 11.\n    - The Reviewer loop paragraph (line ~339) and the Configuration example (line ~400): the root-only `package*.json` becomes `**/package*.json`, `go.mod` becomes `**/go.mod`, and so on. Add one `web/` prefix example.\n    - The doc comment on `config.When`: replace \"Semantics are owned by #15\" with a pointer to `Matches`.\n    - `internal/roles/config.yaml` comments, if any mention `when:`.\n14. **Tests to add** beyond the plan: amendments 1, 2, 3, 5, 6 (a new branch, where `refs/ard/` is absent), 7, 9 (label only, state only), 10, 11 and 12. Also a test that `Matches` is never consulted when the tests failed (`buildWorker` already skips requests then).\n\n\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-23T15:21:58Z\n\n<!-- ard:triage regate body=49101a2bab03 -->\n**ard · triage · paused**\n\nThe title or body of this issue changed after it was admitted for triage, so ard stopped. A maintainer can review the change, re-apply `ard:pending` and remove `ard:needs-human` to continue.\n\n","numLines":99,"startLine":1,"totalLines":99}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EXfNJkFgJEdRyje19WmYK1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
